# ntfy-specific, NON-SECRET config. This file IS committed.
#
# Shared values (TZ/CONFIG_ROOT/ADMIN_DOMAIN) live in ../../common.env.
# Every ntfy setting is passed as an NTFY_* environment variable in
# compose.yaml rather than through a server.yml, to avoid a single-file bind
# mount. The reason is written out there.
#
# ── FIRST DEPLOY IS A 403, AND THAT IS CORRECT ──────────────────────────
#
# NTFY_AUTH_DEFAULT_ACCESS=deny-all means nothing can publish or subscribe
# until a user exists. The web UI will load and every action will fail until
# you run the commands below. There are no users in a fresh auth.db.
#
#   # 1. an admin for yourself (prompts for a password)
#   docker exec -it ntfy ntfy user add --role=admin jj
#
#   # 2. a publish-only account for machines. Netdata, Komodo and Proxmox
#   #    all send alerts; none of them ever need to READ a topic.
#   docker exec -it ntfy ntfy user add --role=user alerts
#   docker exec ntfy ntfy access alerts 'alerts' write-only
#
#   # 3. confirm
#   docker exec ntfy ntfy user list
#   docker exec ntfy ntfy access
#
# The `alerts` password is what goes into each publisher's config. Store it
# as a Komodo secret Variable (NTFY_ALERTS_PASSWORD) when wiring Netdata up,
# the same way every other credential in this repo is handled.
#
# ── ⚠️ NOTIFICATIONS ONLY ARRIVE ON THE TAILNET ─────────────────────────
#
# ntfy is published at ntfy.admin.jjventer.co.za, which is the tailnet-and-LAN
# half of the naming split (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md). The Android app therefore
# only receives while the phone is on the tailnet or at home, because the name
# does not resolve anywhere else and the ISP blocks inbound regardless.
#
# In practice that means Tailscale must stay running in the background on the
# phone. If alerts need to arrive with Tailscale off, ntfy has to move to the
# public *.jjventer.co.za half behind the tunnel, which is a separate decision
# with its own exposure: a public ntfy is a public POST endpoint, and deny-all
# above becomes the only thing standing in front of it.
#
# Left on the admin half deliberately. Infrastructure alerts are infrastructure.

# Nothing else ntfy-specific needed yet.
